  A  item.SerialNumber changes, or item.Object -> a DIFFERENT object
     => SLOT RECYCLED. The object was really destroyed and the index reissued.
  B  item.Object -> 0 (and Flags -> 0), no recycle yet
     => FreeUObjectIndex ran: ~UObjectBase executed. Real destruction.
  C  a new item-flag bit appears before B, and that bit is the one the sweep sees spike
     population-wide  => the REACHABILITY PASS marked it. If we rooted it, the poked bit
     is NOT honoured by this build's GC.
  D  neither the item nor the sweep moves, but the object's vtable/NamePrivate go bad
     => OUT-OF-BAND teardown (package unload / stream-out / explicit destroy), or the
     pointer was never the object we thought. GC was never involved.
  VOID  no target event AND no decoy event => the watcher never showed it can see a change.
